  "id": "COMPOUND:3095 - PROTEIN:6156",
  "verbalization": "Isoliquiritigenin is implicated in the regulation of G2/mitotic-specific cyclin B1 through a multi-step mechanism involving UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10. This enzyme is a common target of multiple compounds, including Isoliquiritigenin, which directly interacts with UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10, suggesting a direct pharmacological interaction. The evidence from the three paths indicates that Isoliquiritigenin may inhibit UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10, which in turn affects the activity of G2/mitotic-specific cyclin B1. The shared target of Isoliquiritigenin and other compounds (Difengpiol A, Sennoside D, and 9-Isovaleroxy Balanophonin) further supports a common pathway in which UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10 acts as a mediator. The integration of these pathways suggests that Isoliquiritigenin may modulate cyclin B1 expression or activity in the G2 phase of the cell cycle, potentially through the regulation of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10. The mechanism is supported by the presence of a consistent target relationship across different compounds, reinforcing the likelihood of a mechanistic link between Isoliquiritigenin and G2/mitotic-specific cyclin B1.",
